    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>, a small Amorite city-state became the master of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in barely a decade of conquest.</li><li>His Code of 282 laws is the most complete legal collection to survive from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#near-east">ancient Near East</a>.</li><li>Lacking strong institutions, the empire fragmented soon after his death and ended with a Hittite raid around 1595 BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> destroyed the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> not by storming it but by damming and then releasing floodwater against it.</p></aside>
    </section>

